NodeScore(score=33.0, feedback='Overall assessment: 33% of requirements satisfied. The code implements a basic SGD-based matrix factorization and includes reproducible splits, initialization, and regularization, but several critical aspects are missing or incomplete for a robust, reproducible, and scalable experiment.\\n\\nFulfilled:\\n- 3) Model implementation: Simple MF with U and V factors and SGD updates; uses biases as optional, which is fine.\\n- 5) Training objective: Regularized MSE with L2 on U and V; SGD updates are performed per rating.\\n- 6) Initialization and regularization: Small random initialization; L2 penalties applied during updates.\\n- 2) Train/test split: Deterministic 80/20 split with fixed seed and separation of train/val, avoiding leakage (for the split, though see caveats below).\\n- 10) Reproducibility: Seeds are used (seed 42 for the split, and a fixed NumPy seed for initialization). Documentation of seeds is present in code.\\n\\nNot fulfilled or incomplete (with concrete improvements):\\n- 1) Data loading and compatibility: No explicit construction of a sparse rating matrix R (users x items) and no support for MovieLens 1M. The implementation loads ratings and builds index mappings but does not store R as a sparse matrix. Recommendation: create a scipy.sparse.csr_matrix R of shape (num_users, num_items) and populate it from the train/val sets. Also add explicit support to download/load ML-1M and parse its ratings format.\\n- 4) Hyperparameters: K, lr, lambda, and epochs exist, but minibatch training is not implemented and there is no explicit early stopping based on validation RMSE. Recommendation: implement minibatch SGD (e.g., batch_size variable) and add optional early stopping that stops when validation RMSE does not improve for a number of epochs.\\n- 7) Handling unseen users/items: The test split uses a union of train and val IDs for mapping, but there is no explicit fallback for unseen users/items at inference time (predict uses