What the implementation does\
- Data loading\
  - Downloads and loads MovieLens data (supports 100k and 1M). It can use LensKit if available, otherwise falls back to manual parsing.\
  - For 100k, it reads user, item, rating, and timestamp; for 1M, it parses ratings.dat with the :: delimiter.\
- Data preparation\
  - Splits the ratings into train/test (80/20 by default). Optional validation split is supported but not used in the shown run.\
  - Builds a single, global set of users and items across all splits and maps them to dense indices for the model.\
- Model: SGD-based matrix factorization with biases\
  - Latent factors: U (user matrix) and V (item matrix), with K latent factors.\
  - Biases: per-user bias bu and per-item bias bi, plus a global mean.\
  - Prediction: rating_hat = global_mean + bu[u] (if user seen in training) + bi[i] (if item seen in training) + dot(U[u], V[i]) (only if both user and item are seen in training).\
  - The model tracks which users/items were seen in training so their biases and latent factors can be updated.\
- Training\
  - Uses SGD with a simple batch loop. For each batch, it accumulates gradients for U, V, bu, and bi and updates parameters with a learning rate (lr) and L2 regularization (reg).\
  - After each epoch, it computes training RMSE and a validation/test RMSE (the code treats the test set as a proxy for validation in the log/output).\
  - Early stopping: stops if no improvement on the \'93validation\'94 RMSE for a number of epochs equal to patience.\
- Evaluation and artifacts\
  - After training, it evaluates the model on the test set to produce test RMSE.\
  - Also computes a baseline RMSE using the global mean as predictor.\
  - Saves artifacts: U, V, bu, bi, and test predictions/truths to the working directory.\
  - Returns a run result with per-epoch RMSEs, best epoch, and RMSEs.\
- Reproducibility\
  - Runs with multiple seeds and latent sizes (K) to explore configurations.\
  - Aggregates results into a single experiment_data.npy file for reproducibility.\
